Subject: missing primary sampling periods in Pcountopen
Message-ID: <vwJjWsxVAek.Qgvi2PUFfRsJ@unmarked.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/unmarked/c/vwJjWsxVAek/m/Qgvi2PUFfRsJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi everyone,
                  I'm using UNMARKED to estimate abundance and detectability of beavers in Patagonia. Every year (primary sampling periods), I conduct 2-3 repeated observations (secondary sampling periods) at the same colonies. However, from year to year some colonies may be abandoned (the whole colony may move somewhere else) and consequently I may lose information for one year.
I was wondering if I can use data on colonies that have been active just for one year, and if they can provide additional data for detection and abundance at that particular period.
In my particular case that will mean that for three years I may have colonies with primary samplings just for one year, sometimes for two and a few times for three years (and of course each year has secondary sampling periods).

Hope my question is easy to understand, otherwise I'd be glad to restate it!

Thanks

Alejandro

