Hi,
I used double sampling to estimate detection probability (note this is distinct from the double observer sampling appoarch; the method is described in MacKenzie and Royle 2005 J App Ecol). This means that I visited 190 sites once, and 10 sites 5 times. I realize this is not ideal, but I'd like to model occupancy using these data.
Is there a way to use unmarked to run occu using these data? I am running into a problem because for 190 rows in my dataframe, there are NA's for 4 of the 5 columns. I assume this is why I get the message: "dims [product 200] do not match the length of object [1000]."
When I run occu for just the 10 rows where I sampled each site evenly it is not problem and the model works fine, but obviously I'd like to run the model using data from all sites.
Has anyone tried to use unmarked for data where they estimated detection probability using a Double Sampling approach? Is there a way to run the model and input a specific detection probability instead of having the program calculate it for you? Does anyone have any suggestions?
Thank you,
Mikey

